Description: the parser of "ls -l" lines (extfs listings, ubsdtar among them, FTP, shell links) read before the name when it was one byte long or empty
Origin: Alpine, https://github.com/alpinelinux/aports/blob/77c6bbe29ea4a9352138b3c974c3926f0ff3635e/main/mc/ticket_4642_parse_ls_vga_fix.patch;
 upstream fixed it otherwise (str_rstrip_eol(): https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/commit/ac9a81d9bd369fc6f571850b90a2f534dc03cc8e,
 30.01.2025, after 4.8.33)
Bug: https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/issues/4642
Why: vfs_parse_ls_lga() stripped the end of line of the name with "--p2 > 0" on a
 size_t: for a name of one byte (or none) p2 went round to SIZE_MAX and the bytes
 before the name were read (undefined behaviour; no visible effect seen). This
 checks the length first, keeping the stripping of up to two \r or \n.

--- lib/vfs/parse_ls_vga.c.orig
+++ lib/vfs/parse_ls_vga.c
@@ -855,13 +855,12 @@ vfs_parse_ls_lga (const char *p, struct stat *s, char **filename, char **linknam
 
     if (t != NULL)
     {
-        size_t p2;
+        size_t p2 = strlen (t);
 
-        p2 = strlen (t);
-        if (--p2 > 0 && (t[p2] == '\r' || t[p2] == '\n'))
-            t[p2] = '\0';
-        if (--p2 > 0 && (t[p2] == '\r' || t[p2] == '\n'))
-            t[p2] = '\0';
+        if (p2 > 0 && (t[p2 - 1] == '\r' || t[p2 - 1] == '\n'))
+            t[--p2] = '\0';
+        if (p2 > 0 && (t[p2 - 1] == '\r' || t[p2 - 1] == '\n'))
+            t[--p2] = '\0';
     }
 
     g_free (p_copy);
